From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:35:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: backup DNS servers, one after another or all at once

When the DNS server does not answer, sing-box answers nothing (AdGuard Home
then waits for its timeout and asks its fallback servers), and an error
answer (SERVFAIL, REFUSED) goes to the client as it is. homeproxy had no
second DNS server for that.

New settings, all off by default (the configuration is then as before):

- routing modes global, gfwlist and proxy_mainland_china (Client
  Settings, under the DNS server): "Backup DNS servers" (none, one after
  another, all at once), "Backup DNS server" (a list in the format of the
  DNS server field, wan included), "Backup DNS servers directly" (ask them
  through direct-out instead of the main node) and "DNS server timeout"
  (seconds, 2 by default);
- custom routing (DNS Settings): the same mode and timeout, and the
  backup servers chosen from the DNS servers (default, system, the
  enabled ones of the DNS Servers tab), in the order of the list.

They are built from the evaluate and respond DNS rules of sing-box 1.14,
after all other DNS rules, so only what no rule answers is affected:
- one after another: the next server is asked when the previous one does
  not answer in the timeout or answers other than NOERROR or NXDOMAIN; the
  last one answers whatever it gets;
- all at once: the first NOERROR or NXDOMAIN answer wins; if none comes,
  the DNS server answers as before.

With these rules sing-box uses its new DNS rule mode and refuses some
older rules (a rule with a strategy, as in the bypass mainland China mode,
where the setting is therefore not offered, or an IP match without
match_response). So the generator asks "sing-box check": if the
configuration with the backup servers is refused and the one without them
is not, they are left out with the reason in the log. On a sing-box older
than 1.14 they are left out with a log line too. A backup server that is
not a DNS address or not a known DNS server is left out or replaced with
default-dns and reported (the guard of patch 015). parse_dnsserver no
longer stops the generator on an address it cannot parse.

Russian translation of the new strings in po/ru (patch 014).

Checked: without the new settings the configuration is byte-identical to
before (24 test configurations, also with the xhttp patch on the official
and the extended core); with them "sing-box check" passes on 1.14.2,
1.14.3 and 1.14.1-extended-2.7.2, and on 1.12.22 and 1.13.21 the backup
servers are left out with a log line. Live with sing-box 1.14.2 and fake
DNS servers (silent, SERVFAIL, REFUSED, NXDOMAIN, a good answer): one
after another moves on after the timeout or at once on SERVFAIL/REFUSED,
stops at NXDOMAIN, the last server answers as it is; all at once returns
the good answer at once even with the first server silent (30 queries in
a row). LuCI: rendered with luci-base in Chromium with a mocked ubus, no
errors on any tab of the client page, the fields show only with their
mode, an invalid address is refused while typing, the saved values are as
entered, and saving without touching them writes the same as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011cyCFAA9hPeqN8wsgkxbrJ
